                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "The game takes us into the Swiss Alps to investigate the mysterious circumstances surrounding our grandfather's death.\n\nThe atmosphere is heavy and captivating. Although the graphics may look a little dated from a technical standpoint, their style with its monochrome and sepia tones, works really well and further enhances the unsettling atmosphere. The world skillfully blends supernatural elements, Alpine folklore and aspects of rural life, giving the game a distinctive identity.\n\nThe story and dialogue are well written, maintaining enough mystery to make you want to uncover more and keep moving forward.\nThe gameplay mechanics are fairly simple, with a strong focus on exploration, finding items and solving a few easy puzzles to progress. The game also features some stealth sections and occasional combat, which I didn't find particularly engaging, although they do add a little variety to the experience.\n\nOverall, I had a great time exploring this world, which I found particularly original. Despite some limitations in its gameplay, I recommend giving this horror adventure a try, especially for its atmosphere and distinctive art direction.",
